# Example apps write artifacts to cwd when run from the repo root.
# (Examples redirect to a temp dir; this is belt-and-suspenders for old runs.)
*-uploads/

# ---- Security: Logs ----
*.log
logs/

# ---- Security: Backups ----
*.bak
*.backup
*.old
*.orig

# ---- Security: Archives (can contain secrets) ----
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# ---- Build artifacts ----
# Canonical output directory for `make build`, `make build-all`,
# `make build-examples`. Anything you `go build` for this repo should land
# here; never commit binaries from the worktree root.
dist/

# Belt-and-braces: still ignore any stray binaries that appear at the root
# from someone running `go build` directly. The convention is `make build`
# → dist/, but ad-hoc builds shouldn't trip the audit either.
demo_server
/gofastr
/gofastr-*
!gofastr/
kiln
kiln-*
!kiln/
/core-ui-demo
/blog
/demo
/website
/site
/widgets-demo
/widgets_demo
# Every examples/<name> builds to /<name> when someone runs `go build
# ./examples/<name>` from the root. Naming them one at a time loses that race
# every time a new example lands — a 12MB embed-demo binary reached a commit
# this way. Ignore the shape instead.
/*-demo
/*-demo-*
# The -demo shape above covers only the examples named that way. Every other
# examples/<name> builds to /<name> too, and naming them one at a time is the
# race that comment warns about — a stray /meridian reached a review this way.
# Regenerate with: ls examples/ | while read d; do [ -d examples/$d ] && echo "/$d"; done
/api-tour
/backoffice
/ecommerce
/lms
/meridian
/portfolio
/project-manager
/real-estate
/spa
/static-site
# Same race for cmd/<name>: `go build ./cmd/repolint` from the root drops a
# 3.5MB binary at /repolint, which is neither a *-demo nor named above. A
# review caught one sitting untracked. Enumerate the package dir, not the
# names — a new cmd/ lands without touching this file.
/bench-resources
/check-csp
/check-embed
/mutate
/repolint
*.png
!assets/brand/*.png
.playwright-mcp/
screens/
research-ui-approaches.md
.mcp.json
# pi agent state (auto-added)
pi-agent/plugins/*
!pi-agent/plugins/registry.json

# kiln per-session journal (write-time state, not source)
.kiln.session.jsonl
.kiln.session.jsonl.bak

# Harness TUI snapshot drift artifacts — the snapshot test writes
# *.txt.new alongside any drifted *.txt for diff inspection. They're
# scratch output, never source. Regenerate the canonical .txt files
# via GOFASTR_UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1.
framework/experimental/harness/client/tui/testdata/snapshots/*.txt.new

# Git worktrees live as sibling directories
worktrees/

# Compiled example binaries (go build output named after the dir).
# Canonical build output is dist/; these are stray local builds.
# (examples/*/site also covers the examples/site/site artifact scrubbed on main.)
examples/*/site
